      "numericalTolerance": 0.0,
      "correctMarks": 4,
      "negativeMarks": 0,
      "solutionHtml": "<p>In $[\\text{Fe}(\\text{CN})_6]^{4-}$, iron is in the $+2$ oxidation state ($3d^6$). Since $\\text{CN}^-$ is a strong-field ligand, all $6$ electrons pair up in the $t_{2g}$ orbitals ($t_{2g}^6 e_g^0$), leaving $0$ unpaired electrons.</p>",
