      "type": "MCQ",
      "difficulty": "hard",
      "revisionZone": "trap_zone",
      "ncertPages": "Class 12, pp. 402-411",
      "statementHtml": "<p>The integrating factor of the linear differential equation $x \\frac{dy}{dx} + 2y = x^2 \\log x$ ($x > 0$) is:</p>",
      "options": [
        { "key": "A", "html": "<p>$e^{2x}$</p>" },
        { "key": "B", "html": "<p>$x^2$</p>" },
        { "key": "C", "html": "<p>$\\frac{1}{x^2}$</p>" },
        { "key": "D", "html": "<p>$2 \\ln x$</p>" }
      ],
      "correctOption": "B",
      "numericalAnswer": null,
      "numericalTolerance": 0.0,
      "correctMarks": 4,
      "negativeMarks": -1,
      "solutionHtml": "<p>Divide by $x$ to put into standard form $\\frac{dy}{dx} + \\frac{2}{x}y = x \\log x$. Here $P(x) = \\frac{2}{x}$, so $$\\text{I.F.} = e^{\\int \\frac{2}{x} dx} = e^{2 \\ln x} = x^2$$</p>",
      "commonMistakeType": "conceptual",
      "hasVideoSolution": true,
      "videoContentId": "vdo_ma_de_01"
    },
