      "revisionZone": "trap_zone",
      "ncertPages": "Class 12 Biology, pp. 99-106",
      "statementHtml": "<p>In prokaryotes like <i>E. coli</i>, the DNA is held with some proteins that are positively charged in a region termed as:</p>",
      "options": [
        { "key": "A", "html": "<p>Nucleosome</p>" },
        { "key": "B", "html": "<p>Nucleoid</p>" },
        { "key": "C", "html": "<p>Chromatin</p>" },
        { "key": "D", "html": "<p>Solenoid</p>" }
      ],
      "correctOption": "B",
      "numericalAnswer": null,
      "numericalTolerance": 0.0,
      "correctMarks": 4,
      "negativeMarks": -1,
      "solutionHtml": "<p>In prokaryotes, negatively charged DNA is held with positively charged non-histone polyamine proteins in a region called the <b>Nucleoid</b> (NCERT Class 12, p. 99).</p>",
      "commonMistakeType": "conceptual",
      "hasVideoSolution": true,
      "videoContentId": "vdo_bio_mol_01"
    },
    {
      "id": "q_neet_2024_bio_03",
      "examId": "neet",
      "exam": "NEET-UG",
      "subjectId": "biology",
      "subject": "Biology",
      "chapterId": "human_physiology",
      "chapter": "Breathing and Exchange of Gases",
      "topicId": "oxygen_dissociation",
      "topic": "Oxygen Dissociation Curve",
      "year": 2024,
      "shift": "05 May Single Shift",
      "type": "MCQ",
      "difficulty": "medium",
      "revisionZone": "high_yield",
      "ncertPages": "Class 11 Biology, pp. 274-276",
      "statementHtml": "<p>Which of the following conditions in the alveoli favors the formation of oxyhaemoglobin ($\\text{HbO}_2$)?</p>",
      "options": [
        { "key": "A", "html": "<p>High $p\\text{O}_2$, low $p\\text{CO}_2$, lesser $\\text{H}^+$ concentration, and lower temperature</p>" },
        { "key": "B", "html": "<p>Low $p\\text{O}_2$, high $p\\text{CO}_2$, higher $\\text{H}^+$ concentration, and higher temperature</p>" },
        { "key": "C", "html": "<p>High $p\\text{O}_2$, high $p\\text{CO}_2$, and lower pH</p>" },
        { "key": "D", "html": "<p>Low $p\\text{O}_2$, low $p\\text{CO}_2$, and higher temperature</p>" }
      ],
      "correctOption": "A",
      "numericalAnswer": null,
      "numericalTolerance": 0.0,
      "correctMarks": 4,
      "negativeMarks": -1,
      "solutionHtml": "<p>In the alveoli, high partial pressure of oxygen ($p\\text{O}_2$), low $p\\text{CO}_2$, lower $\\text{H}^+$ concentration (higher pH), and lower temperature shift the oxygen dissociation curve to the left, favoring oxyhaemoglobin formation (NCERT Class 11, p. 274).</p>",
      "commonMistakeType": "conceptual",
      "hasVideoSolution": true,
      "videoContentId": "vdo_bio_phys_01"
    },
    {
      "id": "q_neet_2024_bio_04",
      "examId": "neet",
      "exam": "NEET-UG",
      "subjectId": "biology",
      "subject": "Biology",
      "chapterId": "principles_inheritance",
      "chapter": "Principles of Inheritance and Variation",
      "topicId": "mendelian_genetics",
      "topic": "Dihybrid Cross & Independent Assortment",
      "year": 2024,
      "shift": "05 May Single Shift",
      "type": "MCQ",
      "difficulty": "easy",
      "revisionZone": "must_revise",
      "ncertPages": "Class 12 Biology, pp. 78-82",
      "statementHtml": "<p>In a standard Mendelian dihybrid cross between two doubly heterozygous pea plants ($RrYy \\times RrYy$), what fraction of the $F_2$ progeny is homozygous recessive for both traits ($rryy$)?</p>",
      "options": [
        { "key": "A", "html": "<p>$\\frac{9}{16}$</p>" },
        { "key": "B", "html": "<p>$\\frac{3}{16}$</p>" },
        { "key": "C", "html": "<p>$\\frac{1}{16}$</p>" },
        { "key": "D", "html": "<p>$\\frac{1}{4}$</p>" }
      ],
      "correctOption": "C",
      "numericalAnswer": null,
      "numericalTolerance": 0.0,
      "correctMarks": 4,
      "negativeMarks": -1,
      "solutionHtml": "<p>In a dihybrid cross $RrYy \\times RrYy$, the phenotypic ratio is $9:3:3:1$, and the probability of obtaining $rryy$ is $\\frac{1}{4} \\times \\frac{1}{4} = \\frac{1}{16}$.</p>",
      "commonMistakeType": "silly",
      "hasVideoSolution": true,
      "videoContentId": "vdo_bio_gen_01"
    }
  ],
